       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **What was written:** metformin 2550 mg three times daily, which is **7,650 mg/day**.\n- **Why it's a problem:** the maximum recommended metformin dose is 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). This order is three times that, and it carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis.\n- **Likely intent:** 2,550 mg is the daily maximum, so you may have meant **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which totals 2,550 mg/day.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n1. Metformin **850 mg** PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day).\n2. A different dose. Give me the per-dose amount and frequency.\n3. The original 2,550 mg TID order, if it's intentional. I'd need you to confirm that explicitly.\n\nI'll enter the order once you confirm."
