       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Metformin 2,550 mg three times daily is 7,650 mg/day, three times the maximum daily dose. I don't know of any indication that supports it, and it risks severe lactic acidosis even with normal kidney and liver function. I'd rather not put a dose in the system that I expect to harm the patient.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals.** This gives 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum. I can enter it right away.\n- **A lower or titrated dose.** For example, start at 500 mg BID with meals and increase gradually.\n- **Pharmacy or a second prescriber.** If you do have a specific reason for this dose, they can review it and enter it through the hospital's high-dose override process.\n\nTell me which one you want and I'll enter it."
